WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:13.013
[rock music playing]

00:45.045 --> 00:47.173
I want to understand irrational numbers.

00:49.508 --> 00:51.343
[Eui-ju] Understand? Me?

00:52.595 --> 00:53.596
Why?

00:54.430 --> 00:55.431
Why?

00:55.514 --> 00:56.557
Why what?

00:56.640 --> 00:59.185
CHAPTER 29: SOMETIMES,
THE TRUTH CAN BE DANGEROUS

01:00.853 --> 01:02.646
Uh… Why…

01:04.273 --> 01:08.444
Why is it that
Pythagoras killed his student in the end?

01:11.739 --> 01:12.990
Don't you get it?

01:13.574 --> 01:17.495
Pythagoras couldn't stand the thought that
his world could collapse in a second.

01:19.872 --> 01:21.540
5TH CENTURY BC

01:21.624 --> 01:22.917
[playful music plays]

01:23.000 --> 01:24.293
[exhales sharply]

01:25.836 --> 01:27.922
-[gasps]
-What's the matter?

01:28.923 --> 01:29.924
[stutters] Master.

01:30.007 --> 01:31.217
PYTHAGOREAN MATH ACADEMY
CROTON, GREECE

01:31.300 --> 01:32.301
Have you…

01:32.384 --> 01:33.385
PYTHAGORAS, DIRECTOR

01:33.469 --> 01:35.095
…perhaps discovered something new?

01:36.138 --> 01:37.765
HIPPASUS, STUDENT

01:37.848 --> 01:39.558
I tried to express

01:40.351 --> 01:42.937
the length of the diagonal
of a unit square.

01:43.813 --> 01:46.440
And I tried to do it as a fraction.

01:46.524 --> 01:49.985
That's right. Every number can
be expressed as a ratio of integers.

01:50.069 --> 01:51.946
It's the absolute truth we teach.

01:52.029 --> 01:53.030
[Eui-ju] Well…

01:55.324 --> 01:57.284
It's just that, it doesn't work.

01:57.368 --> 01:59.036
-[sighs]
-What's that?

01:59.578 --> 02:00.663
The thing is

02:01.497 --> 02:03.749
this number cannot be expressed
as a fraction!

02:04.542 --> 02:05.584
Wait.

02:06.502 --> 02:09.255
Wait a minute. [breathing shakily]

02:11.340 --> 02:12.591
All right.

02:12.675 --> 02:13.676
Prove it to me.

02:14.635 --> 02:15.970
-[playful music plays]
-Okay.

02:16.887 --> 02:18.097
Okay.

02:20.724 --> 02:21.851
Got a square.

02:22.518 --> 02:23.519
Please watch.

02:30.109 --> 02:31.110
-[sighs]
-[buzzer sounds]

02:31.193 --> 02:32.653
I can't express it.

02:33.153 --> 02:34.405
-[sobbing] I just can't.
-[gasps]

02:38.909 --> 02:40.119
If you're right then,

02:40.786 --> 02:43.873
it means everything we've believed
up until now is just wrong.

02:47.751 --> 02:48.752
Have you…

02:50.671 --> 02:51.922
told anyone else about this?

02:53.048 --> 02:54.049
I haven't.

02:54.550 --> 02:56.385
I haven't told anyone else about it yet.

02:56.468 --> 02:58.137
I wanted to tell you first, master.

03:00.264 --> 03:01.557
[sighs] I see.

03:02.266 --> 03:03.309
That's a relief.

03:05.644 --> 03:07.104
Hippasus.

03:10.107 --> 03:11.108
Yes?

03:11.692 --> 03:12.943
Your proof

03:14.153 --> 03:16.697
-never existed in the first place.
-[dramatic music plays]

03:17.865 --> 03:20.075
[grunting] Master.

03:20.159 --> 03:23.996
The truth can be far too dangerous.

03:25.998 --> 03:27.166
[echoes] Master!

03:33.088 --> 03:34.298
[sighs]

03:34.381 --> 03:37.718
Irrational numbers meant the collapse
of his entire world.

03:40.429 --> 03:42.848
[Eui-ju sighs] He's such a math geek.

03:42.932 --> 03:46.060
His eyes light up
whenever he talks about math. It's freaky.

03:47.353 --> 03:48.354
Man.

03:51.023 --> 03:52.358
But then again…

03:53.776 --> 03:57.279
[sighs] …it's kind of cool.

04:04.620 --> 04:06.038
[yelps]

04:06.872 --> 04:07.873
Are you okay?

04:10.250 --> 04:13.379
[stutters] Y-Yes. I'm… I'm okay. [grunts]

04:14.213 --> 04:16.340
That's why you shouldn't space out
when you walk.

04:17.091 --> 04:18.092
Right.

04:18.759 --> 04:20.010
How embarrassing.

04:20.094 --> 04:22.721
That doesn't count as embarrassing to you,
does it?

04:26.141 --> 04:30.145
They say doing something embarrassing
boosts your creativity.

04:30.229 --> 04:31.522
Ah.

04:31.605 --> 04:34.817
So you're intentionally embarrassing
yourself? Is there anything more?

04:35.651 --> 04:37.987
It's not embarrassing
if I tell you in advance.

04:38.070 --> 04:40.114
I see. Go for the boost then.

04:40.739 --> 04:41.907
I'm rooting for you.

04:47.204 --> 04:48.205
EPISODE 9

04:48.288 --> 04:49.456
I'm home.

04:50.165 --> 04:52.292
[Ma] Oh! Go to the bathroom first.

04:52.376 --> 04:54.461
-[people talking on television]
-Huh? I'm okay.

04:55.170 --> 04:57.214
You can hardly do number two
when you're out.

04:57.297 --> 05:00.509
So the moment you come home, you have
to go straight to the bathroom, okay?

05:00.592 --> 05:03.429
And hey. [clicks tongue]
If you need to go, don't hold it.

05:03.512 --> 05:05.389
Just please make sure you go.

05:06.181 --> 05:08.142
[grunts] Okay!

05:08.225 --> 05:09.852
I can take care of it myself.

05:09.935 --> 05:11.895
You don't have to tell me
even when I have to poop.

05:11.979 --> 05:14.690
It's because you can't take care of it
on your own! [clicks tongue]

05:16.442 --> 05:17.609
Okay!

05:18.444 --> 05:19.445
I'll go.

05:20.362 --> 05:21.363
Geez.

05:21.447 --> 05:24.199
Maybe I should pay a personal visit
to your homeroom teacher.

05:25.075 --> 05:26.243
[stutters] Why?

05:27.494 --> 05:30.039
He carried you all the way to the ER
on his back.

05:30.122 --> 05:32.583
That's something to be awfully sorry
and grateful for.

05:33.292 --> 05:34.960
Oh, no. There's no need to.

05:35.044 --> 05:36.211
I told him I was grateful.

05:36.295 --> 05:38.255
And he's busy.
Don't ever reach out to him or anything.

05:38.338 --> 05:39.631
Don't do it ever, never!

05:40.299 --> 05:42.051
You're afraid of him, aren't you?

05:42.801 --> 05:45.220
Fair enough.
Judging by all the demerits you got,

05:45.721 --> 05:47.097
no wonder you're scared of him.

05:47.181 --> 05:49.475
[chuckles] Man,
that teacher must be brutal.

05:50.184 --> 05:51.935
You really got on his bad side.

05:52.519 --> 05:54.772
No, I mean… It's not that bad.

05:54.855 --> 05:57.483
He's just a little…
a little blunt, I guess?

05:57.566 --> 06:00.027
He can be kind of prickly sometimes.

06:00.110 --> 06:03.447
But the truth is that
he's truly good at heart, you know?

06:03.530 --> 06:06.158
He's immature and childish at times.

06:06.241 --> 06:07.701
But he is truly good at heart.

06:08.327 --> 06:09.328
Heart.

06:10.204 --> 06:11.497
[playful music plays]

06:20.214 --> 06:21.381
[dog whines]

06:26.845 --> 06:28.680
-[owl hooting]
-[exhales]

06:30.015 --> 06:31.100
I get it.

06:31.183 --> 06:34.645
Smart people are known to be good
at manipulating others however they want.

06:35.562 --> 06:36.897
That makes sense.

06:36.980 --> 06:39.191
I have been manipulated.

06:39.274 --> 06:41.235
I've been manipulated just like Mr. Yoon.

06:42.277 --> 06:44.029
After nagging and scolding you ten times,

06:44.113 --> 06:45.656
they say one nice thing,
and then you're like,

06:45.739 --> 06:48.117
"Oh? Maybe they're actually
a good person after all."

06:48.200 --> 06:50.577
Yeah, that's exactly how it works.
[chuckles]

06:54.414 --> 06:56.333
Really. He's so mean to me all the time,

06:56.416 --> 06:58.168
but I suddenly have butterflies
in my stomach

06:58.252 --> 07:00.045
just because he said
he'd try to understand me?

07:00.129 --> 07:01.171
It's ridiculous!

07:01.672 --> 07:03.132
[sighs]

07:06.176 --> 07:08.428
You better snap out of it, Yeo Eui-ju.

07:08.512 --> 07:11.181
Don't even make eye contact
with Math from tomorrow on.

07:15.435 --> 07:18.730
CHAPTER 30: SOMEONE
I SHOULDN'T AND CAN'T LIKE

07:22.442 --> 07:25.445
Hey, guys.
Did you read the article I sent?

07:25.529 --> 07:27.114
Professor Na Deul-i

07:27.739 --> 07:30.742
has been named the First-ever
Korean Recipient of the Fields Medal.

07:30.826 --> 07:31.910
What about it?

07:32.661 --> 07:33.996
Do you know her?

07:34.079 --> 07:35.414
No, I don't.

07:35.497 --> 07:36.790
But Woo-su does.

07:37.624 --> 07:38.876
Oh!

07:38.959 --> 07:40.836
She was his Olympiad mate
from middle school.

07:40.919 --> 07:41.962
Really?

07:42.045 --> 07:43.046
[Dong-ju] Really?

07:43.130 --> 07:44.631
Aren't you jealous?

07:45.174 --> 07:47.301
Don't you think that
it should've been you?

07:50.095 --> 07:52.764
[sighs] If you hadn't given up
on that Olympiad.

07:54.016 --> 07:55.851
Actually, only if you had
gone and studied abroad…

07:55.934 --> 07:57.811
-[Gi-jeon clears throat]
-Stop it, Da-ju.

07:58.604 --> 08:00.022
Listen, I always knew he'd make it.

08:00.105 --> 08:02.941
I just never thought he'd be here
eating toast with me

08:03.025 --> 08:04.735
and arguing with those math dropouts.

08:05.694 --> 08:07.905
-I'm talking about my friend, Ga Woo-su.
-[Gi-jeon sighs]

08:07.988 --> 08:09.948
Ga Woo-su, my genius friend!

08:12.201 --> 08:13.911
[sighs] Whatever.

08:14.536 --> 08:15.746
If he'd brought glory to Korea

08:15.829 --> 08:17.372
-by winning a Fields Medal--
-Stop.

08:17.456 --> 08:18.916
Shut it. [clicks tongue]

08:19.875 --> 08:21.835
So what if that professor won the medal?

08:25.047 --> 08:26.048
Hey.

08:26.590 --> 08:28.592
Do you even know what a Fields Medal is?

08:29.676 --> 08:30.928
I do. And?

08:31.011 --> 08:33.889
Then why don't you tell me who
the very first Fields Medal winner was.

08:38.685 --> 08:40.687
-David Copperfield.
-[sighs] I'm done.

08:40.771 --> 08:43.106
I refuse to waste my words on someone
who doesn't know that.

08:43.190 --> 08:44.316
[Gi-jeon scoffs]

08:44.399 --> 08:45.984
Anyway, Woo-su…

08:48.153 --> 08:49.696
[sighs] I'm done talking to you too.

08:50.322 --> 08:51.406
Enjoy your breakfast.

08:59.790 --> 09:01.708
I wonder when he'll head out.

09:01.792 --> 09:02.793
[giggles]

09:03.293 --> 09:05.045
He usually comes out around this time.

09:05.712 --> 09:08.715
Did I forget anything?
Did I forget all my textbooks?

09:08.799 --> 09:10.634
I should grab my puffer. [chuckles]

09:10.717 --> 09:13.387
Why isn't he coming out?
We're gonna be late. [chuckles]

09:13.470 --> 09:14.680
[Gi-jeon, Da-ju speaking]

09:14.763 --> 09:17.683
[Gi-jeon] Da-ju, hurry up!
It's been an hour since Woo-su left!

09:17.766 --> 09:19.851
-[Da-ju] He's driving me nuts.
-What the heck?

09:19.935 --> 09:21.728
-[Eui-ju] What time is it?
-Hurry up. We're late.

09:22.229 --> 09:23.897
[groans] He's always like this.

09:24.940 --> 09:25.941
Isn't that Eui-ju?

09:27.025 --> 09:28.318
It's Eui-ju.

09:28.402 --> 09:29.403
She's late too.

09:34.533 --> 09:37.077
[students] Good morning.

09:37.160 --> 09:38.537
Hello.

09:39.538 --> 09:42.332
[Eui-ju] Why does he
flip his hair like that?

09:42.416 --> 09:43.834
Let's get started right away.

09:45.210 --> 09:47.087
[Eui-ju] Why does he roll up his sleeve?

09:49.589 --> 09:51.216
Why are his fingers so long?

09:51.300 --> 09:52.426
[gentle music playing]

10:00.350 --> 10:01.768
[chuckles]

10:03.353 --> 10:05.814
Why does he drink water like that?

10:09.067 --> 10:10.277
[sighs]

10:10.360 --> 10:11.903
He's spinning his pen.

10:14.323 --> 10:16.033
He's so… [inhales]

10:17.576 --> 10:18.577
He's so…

10:19.202 --> 10:20.245
so annoying.

10:22.164 --> 10:23.165
[grunts]

10:23.665 --> 10:25.792
What is it that you wanna tell me?

10:26.376 --> 10:27.586
Come and sit here first.

10:31.048 --> 10:32.049
[sighs]

10:32.799 --> 10:33.800
Go-ya.

10:33.884 --> 10:38.180
You know that fangirling used to be
my only joy in life.

10:38.847 --> 10:39.848
I know.

10:41.016 --> 10:44.811
Of course, I am aware that
they were all from a different world,

10:44.895 --> 10:46.813
but my love for every one of them

10:46.897 --> 10:49.316
was always honest and real.

10:49.900 --> 10:51.860
Thinking about those characters

10:51.943 --> 10:53.779
gave me the strength to keep going.

10:54.863 --> 10:55.864
But now…

10:56.615 --> 10:58.867
every time he crosses my mind…

11:00.827 --> 11:03.413
Oh, geez! I get so mad!

11:04.081 --> 11:05.082
[grunts]

11:05.582 --> 11:07.000
I really don't wanna think about him.

11:07.084 --> 11:09.378
I'm not supposed to think about him.

11:10.003 --> 11:11.338
But he's stuck in my head.

11:13.215 --> 11:14.257
You're just in denial.

11:15.842 --> 11:16.843
In denial?

11:16.927 --> 11:18.428
You've always been like that.

11:18.512 --> 11:22.015
You watch idol videos all the time
but say you're not a fan.

11:22.557 --> 11:24.810
And you keep saving pictures
of that lead drama actor

11:24.893 --> 11:26.812
but claim
it's because he's good at acting.

11:28.021 --> 11:30.232
Do I do that?

11:30.315 --> 11:31.942
Mmm… You do.

11:32.776 --> 11:35.821
You're already head over heels for him
but you're trying to deny it.

11:35.904 --> 11:38.532
Your words say otherwise, but
your heart is already racing toward him.

11:38.615 --> 11:40.075
No, I can't.

11:41.368 --> 11:42.828
I can't.

11:43.412 --> 11:46.206
I can't! I shouldn't like him.
I simply can't!

11:46.873 --> 11:47.874
I just can't.

11:48.583 --> 11:50.752
Why? Huh?

11:52.379 --> 11:54.798
Why can't you like the PE teacher?

11:55.715 --> 11:56.716
[owl hooting]

11:59.302 --> 12:00.303
Huh?

12:01.471 --> 12:04.057
Why would you deny having a crush
on the PE teacher?

12:04.141 --> 12:05.350
[intriguing music plays]

12:05.934 --> 12:06.935
Oh…

12:09.396 --> 12:10.772
No, that's not it.

12:10.856 --> 12:12.149
No.

12:12.983 --> 12:14.067
-Let's go?
-Huh?

12:14.151 --> 12:15.694
Never mind what I said. Come on.

12:15.777 --> 12:17.571
-Huh?
-Come on. Let's go.

12:19.114 --> 12:20.240
-Hey.
-Hi.

12:20.323 --> 12:21.450
Jenny, where are you going?

12:21.533 --> 12:22.784
Oh, teachers' office.

12:22.868 --> 12:25.787
I'm asking for permission
to go tour the city.

12:25.871 --> 12:27.622
Good for you. Where are you going?

12:27.706 --> 12:30.542
Oh. I'm going to go
to the Gyeongbokgung Palace in hanbok.

12:30.625 --> 12:32.085
And then the market.

12:32.169 --> 12:34.129
I'm going
to have gimbap and tteokbokki there.

12:34.212 --> 12:37.299
Hongdae too. After Hongdae, I'm going
to the Han River to have ramyeon.

12:37.382 --> 12:38.800
And then N Seoul Tower too.

12:39.843 --> 12:41.136
Wow.

12:41.219 --> 12:44.723
You've got that much energy
to go to all those places?

12:44.806 --> 12:45.974
-Mm-hmm.
-Jenny,

12:46.057 --> 12:48.768
you know you have to write
a field trip report afterwards, right?

12:48.852 --> 12:50.812
Of course, I do.

12:50.896 --> 12:53.565
"I have learned a lot
about Korean culture."

12:53.648 --> 12:55.609
I just need to write it like that, right?

12:55.692 --> 12:56.693
[chuckles] Bye!

12:58.528 --> 13:01.781
She just… She has no idea
what the requirements are.

13:02.365 --> 13:04.242
Let's just leave her be. She seems happy.

13:04.326 --> 13:05.744
[sighs] Oh, boy.

13:05.827 --> 13:07.704
THE DANCING CARNATION
NOTABLE WORK "MY MOTHER"

13:07.787 --> 13:08.788
BY YOON DONG-JU

13:22.928 --> 13:24.179
Wow.

13:24.262 --> 13:28.099
You're reading that book again?
You must know all the lines.

13:28.183 --> 13:29.184
[whispers] Yes, I do.

13:29.809 --> 13:34.814
"The face, which no longer smiled,
was embracing a flower in full bloom."

13:35.524 --> 13:39.778
If she no longer smiles, maybe
it means Dong-ju's mother passed away.

13:39.861 --> 13:42.489
When he writes,
"And a small flower with no answer,"

13:42.572 --> 13:45.742
it must mean that the small flower
is Dong-ju.

13:47.160 --> 13:49.871
But why didn't he answer
when his mother called for him?

13:50.372 --> 13:52.874
-Why didn't he look at her?
-[sighs]

13:52.958 --> 13:54.793
He probably resented his mother.

13:54.876 --> 13:58.421
[sobbing] I bet he probably regrets it
so much now.

14:00.048 --> 14:01.049
Man,

14:01.758 --> 14:05.428
you would've gotten a perfect score
on Korean lit if you studied like that.

14:07.013 --> 14:08.682
How is the poem coming along?

14:09.808 --> 14:10.809
Well…

14:14.229 --> 14:15.772
Hey. [mouthing]

14:19.276 --> 14:20.694
Hello.

14:25.198 --> 14:27.117
[gentle music plays]

14:41.923 --> 14:44.134
[somber music plays]

15:05.780 --> 15:06.781
Go-ya.

15:06.865 --> 15:08.658
Why didn't you come and talk to Mr. Yoon?

15:11.036 --> 15:12.871
You've gotten really close.

15:14.497 --> 15:15.498
What?

15:15.582 --> 15:18.293
No, he gave me some feedback
about my poem.

15:28.637 --> 15:30.597
I shouldn't like him, I simply can't.

15:31.264 --> 15:32.265
I just can't.

15:41.274 --> 15:43.485
That's why you shouldn't space out
when you walk.

15:45.195 --> 15:46.571
His voice,

15:47.322 --> 15:50.325
you could totally hear the concern
in his voice.

15:50.825 --> 15:51.868
[chuckles]

15:54.788 --> 15:56.623
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 6

15:59.709 --> 16:02.712
[Young-hee] You're supposed to be
running this company someday. But now?

16:03.213 --> 16:04.589
What is this I hear

16:05.674 --> 16:07.592
about you and some guy?

16:07.676 --> 16:09.511
Have you lost your mind?

16:09.594 --> 16:11.888
Who told you that? Tell me!

16:16.893 --> 16:18.144
I did. Ju Si-on.

16:19.938 --> 16:21.272
It was all for your sake.

16:22.065 --> 16:23.274
It was you?

16:24.818 --> 16:25.860
Is this why you joined the company?

16:25.944 --> 16:28.697
To win my mother's favor
and just tell her about Yoon and me?

16:28.780 --> 16:29.864
[Da-ju scoffs]

16:29.948 --> 16:31.908
Honestly, I did it for your future.

16:33.410 --> 16:35.787
You're a man with a great future. [scoffs]

16:36.454 --> 16:39.374
You can't afford to be the subject
of any gossip.

16:39.457 --> 16:41.334
-Don't make me laugh.
-[chuckles]

16:41.418 --> 16:44.379
Yoon is never gonna choose you,
even if you tear us apart.

16:44.462 --> 16:45.714
He was the first

16:46.840 --> 16:47.924
who laughed at my joke.

16:48.007 --> 16:49.217
There's no way.

16:49.968 --> 16:53.096
You see. Yoon laughed at all my jokes.

16:53.179 --> 16:55.098
He probably just did it
so you wouldn't feel embarrassed.

16:55.181 --> 16:57.225
Oh, no. Oh, no.

16:57.851 --> 16:58.852
You don't get it.

16:58.935 --> 17:02.647
The way Yoon looks at me is completely
different from the way he looks

17:02.731 --> 17:04.065
at anyone else.

17:04.149 --> 17:05.525
-It's the same.
-No, it's not.

17:05.608 --> 17:07.152
-It's the same.
-No…

17:08.820 --> 17:10.905
You can take it out on me all you want.

17:10.989 --> 17:12.782
But if you mess with him, I won't have it.

17:12.866 --> 17:14.159
[scoffs]

17:17.036 --> 17:19.622
-No, you're not going anywhere.
-Move.

17:19.706 --> 17:22.083
No way. I'll never let you… [shrieks]

17:22.167 --> 17:24.919
-Mr. Kim!
-[Kim] Yes, Madam Chairman!

17:28.173 --> 17:32.469
Tie him up and don't let him go until you
handle Choi Yoon or whatever his name is.

17:35.889 --> 17:38.016
-Get off me. Get off!
-[groans]

17:40.143 --> 17:41.394
[groans]

17:43.188 --> 17:44.189
[shouts]

17:45.231 --> 17:46.232
[Young-hee] Get him!

17:49.611 --> 17:51.905
[tires squealing]

17:57.535 --> 17:59.078
[grunting]

18:08.630 --> 18:10.131
[laughing]

18:46.251 --> 18:47.293
[panting]

18:51.464 --> 18:52.465
Are you okay?

18:53.049 --> 18:55.385
This is why I told you never to be alone,
Choi Yoon!

18:56.803 --> 18:57.846
Are you not hurt?

19:06.521 --> 19:07.522
Let's go.

19:15.446 --> 19:16.990
[gasps]

19:19.492 --> 19:21.494
Oh! What am I doing?

19:23.037 --> 19:25.707
[breathes shakily] Why…
Why did I turn into Yoon?

19:25.790 --> 19:27.083
Why did I turn into Mr. Yoon?

19:28.543 --> 19:30.420
It's so smooth. Why is it so vivid?

19:32.213 --> 19:33.339
Could this be…

19:35.008 --> 19:36.342
[playful music plays]

19:36.426 --> 19:37.468
Oh.

19:41.014 --> 19:44.309
TOPOLOGY OF ALGEBRAIC CURVES
AND SURFACES

19:50.064 --> 19:51.649
HEY, IT'S BEEN A WHILE

19:51.733 --> 19:53.735
I'M BACK IN KOREA
CAN WE MEET UP?

19:58.948 --> 20:00.450
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

20:06.789 --> 20:08.750
[pensive music plays]

20:08.833 --> 20:09.959
[no audible dialogue]

20:17.550 --> 20:18.551
Okay.

20:24.307 --> 20:25.683
Huh? Go-ya.

20:29.771 --> 20:31.064
I need to talk to you.

20:38.696 --> 20:40.239
What was that just now?

20:40.323 --> 20:44.369
Oh. You mean that I told him I was
having trouble coming up with a title

20:44.452 --> 20:45.453
for the poem.

20:45.536 --> 20:48.790
So he said that I should try using
the first image that comes to mind

20:48.873 --> 20:51.209
or a word that shows up a lot in the poem.

20:51.292 --> 20:54.462
So I just asked him
to please check a few options for me.

20:54.545 --> 20:56.047
And why did you go alone?

20:56.130 --> 20:57.256
You could've invited me.

20:58.424 --> 21:03.137
Well, I was going to. But I decided to go
alone because it wasn't a big deal.

21:03.763 --> 21:05.098
"Not a big deal"?

21:06.349 --> 21:09.769
I'm always too nervous to even
bring myself to say hello to Dong-ju.

21:09.852 --> 21:13.147
But laughing and talking with him
is not a big deal to you?

21:13.773 --> 21:14.983
[wistful music plays]

21:17.193 --> 21:18.778
Oh, that's…

21:18.861 --> 21:19.946
Be honest with me.

21:20.822 --> 21:22.365
Mr. Jung's not your crush is he?

21:23.199 --> 21:24.450
You have a crush on Dong-ju.

21:26.160 --> 21:27.161
What are you talking about?

21:27.245 --> 21:28.538
I know you do.

21:28.621 --> 21:30.581
Otherwise, why would you go alone
to talk to him?

21:31.165 --> 21:32.375
Why would you be in denial?

21:34.836 --> 21:36.629
[sighs] No.

21:36.713 --> 21:38.756
I wasn't talking about Mr. Yoon.

21:42.510 --> 21:44.262
[sighs] Ah…

21:44.345 --> 21:47.640
Why can't you just…
just say something to me then?

21:47.724 --> 21:50.351
Anyone can see
you're acting suspicious right now.

21:52.437 --> 21:53.438
[sighs]

21:54.063 --> 21:55.106
Can't you trust me?

21:57.066 --> 21:59.569
-What?
-Why can't you believe me.

21:59.652 --> 22:01.029
I already said no.

22:01.571 --> 22:03.656
Have I ever lied to you
about anything before?

22:05.199 --> 22:06.284
[sighs]

22:07.326 --> 22:08.327
Fine.

22:09.078 --> 22:10.079
Let's go with that.

22:10.163 --> 22:13.624
I'm just so blinded by a man that
I can't trust my innocent friend.

22:17.420 --> 22:18.588
[sighs]

22:22.633 --> 22:25.011
-It wouldn't be me, right? It wasn't…
-It was me. I did it.

22:25.094 --> 22:26.095
Did you get choco balls?

22:26.179 --> 22:27.221
Whatever.

22:35.938 --> 22:36.939
Hey.

22:37.565 --> 22:38.566
What's wrong with her?

22:43.154 --> 22:45.573
-You think they had a fight?
-They definitely had a fight.

22:45.656 --> 22:46.741
I think so.

22:46.824 --> 22:48.242
-[Dan-ji] Geez.
-It's so weird.

22:50.495 --> 22:51.537
[sighs]

22:56.375 --> 22:57.376
[grunts]

22:58.294 --> 23:00.129
[sighs]

23:01.964 --> 23:03.257
[somber music plays]

23:08.346 --> 23:10.848
I hope she won't be angry too long.

23:13.726 --> 23:14.727
[sighs]

23:28.116 --> 23:33.204
CHAPTER 31:
EVERYONE HAS A SPECIAL SOMEONE

23:45.466 --> 23:46.467
[sniffs]

23:48.469 --> 23:49.554
Oh.

23:50.179 --> 23:51.180
What the heck?

23:52.723 --> 23:56.352
Why am I waiting for Math
when Mr. Jung walked out of his house?

23:57.270 --> 23:58.271
[gasps]

23:58.771 --> 24:00.106
Oh, no.

24:00.189 --> 24:03.025
When I look at his face, it feels…

24:03.109 --> 24:04.569
Are you okay?

24:05.611 --> 24:06.654
[gasps]

24:07.321 --> 24:08.406
[grunts]

24:09.031 --> 24:10.032
No way.

24:27.800 --> 24:29.886
[Go-ya] Love is like first snow.

24:30.386 --> 24:31.512
Right in that moment.

24:32.013 --> 24:33.181
When you see them…

24:33.681 --> 24:36.517
Oh! And you know they're the one.

24:37.059 --> 24:39.061
It always comes when you least expect it.

24:42.190 --> 24:43.566
MINI MOCK EXAMINATION 7

24:47.945 --> 24:49.947
[Eui-Ju] My first love.

24:50.531 --> 24:52.783
My first love is Math and not PE?

24:55.161 --> 24:56.245
What do I do?

24:57.955 --> 25:00.958
What do I do? What do I do?

25:06.881 --> 25:07.965
[phone buzzes]

25:08.049 --> 25:09.508
[barista] Your large mocha's ready.

25:11.594 --> 25:13.179
Thank you. Enjoy your coffee.

25:13.262 --> 25:14.889
Thank you very much.

25:14.972 --> 25:16.098
[sighs]

25:26.859 --> 25:27.860
Oh.

25:32.531 --> 25:33.532
[chuckles]

25:34.033 --> 25:35.034
What the heck?

25:35.868 --> 25:37.203
What is he doing here?

25:38.537 --> 25:39.705
[gasps]

25:39.789 --> 25:41.040
Why didn't I see him earlier?

25:41.123 --> 25:42.124
Hold on.

25:42.208 --> 25:45.628
When I ordered this,
I was up at the counter.

25:46.379 --> 25:48.339
[chuckles] Oh man. [laughs]

25:49.048 --> 25:51.217
Wait. Uh… Hold on.

25:51.300 --> 25:53.427
Did he know I was here,
that I like this place?

25:53.511 --> 25:54.762
Oh, my…

25:54.845 --> 25:56.222
[clears throat] Maybe not.

25:57.473 --> 26:00.059
Is this what people call destiny?
[chuckles]

26:03.104 --> 26:04.105
What's that?

26:06.607 --> 26:07.733
Is that a mocha?

26:11.070 --> 26:12.071
[gasps]

26:12.154 --> 26:14.949
-[Woo-su chuckles]
-[chuckles] It's so not like him.

26:15.700 --> 26:18.119
And he added so much whipped cream on top.

26:18.202 --> 26:21.122
Oh, please. It looks just like mine.

26:21.789 --> 26:22.790
What's with him?

26:26.502 --> 26:29.005
Huh? Why is he waving his hand?

26:29.088 --> 26:30.589
[door opens]

26:33.426 --> 26:34.844
[person chuckles]

26:34.927 --> 26:36.012
[wistful music plays]

26:38.889 --> 26:40.016
Been a while.

26:40.099 --> 26:42.560
-I've missed you so much.
-[both chuckle]

26:45.187 --> 26:48.065
[Eui-ju] I really didn't know
what to make of my feelings.

26:48.816 --> 26:49.817
But then

26:50.735 --> 26:52.445
it all became very clear.

26:56.032 --> 27:01.078
What those reckless, aimless feelings
of mine had really been all along.

27:03.372 --> 27:04.790
Everyone has someone like that,

27:06.292 --> 27:07.376
at least once,

27:08.377 --> 27:11.547
someone who can make
your heart suddenly drop.
